{"conversation_id":"29f740e7-285e-4b94-a559-27455325c321","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I am reading the dispatching brief, current REPL store and main modules, DHT composition docs, and Gambit capability/C4/P1e records to analyze the five design decisions for in-session `dao.jing` store switching.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-22 15:33:50 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-22 22:33:50 ICT (+07)\n\n### Decision Verdicts\n\n1. **Swap semantics for the live VM**: **(a) Quiesce** — require a clean or freshly `(reset)` session (`:quiesced? true`, no parked run, no unwritten rows or pending publications) before swapping, and rebuild the session over the target store's own validated `:recovery` snapshot with no cross-store index copy (also fixing `yin.repl/rebuild-session` and `(vm ...)` to check `store/retain-on-reset?` rather than `store/durable?`).\n2. **Ordering**: **`open-first` (strict, unconditional)** — parse, validate, lock, recover, and compose the new store and transport session completely before closing the old transport session and store handle, so any open failure leaves the old store and session untouched.\n3. **Meaning for `dht:`**: **Full composition lifecycle transition** — swapping into `dht:\u003cdir\u003e` accepts keyword join options (`:peers`/`:peer`, `:listen`/`:bind`/`:port`, `:publish`, `:key`, `:principals`/`:principal`, `:trust`, `:follow`, `:join`), prints the disclosure banner, installs DHT host modules and link source, and attaches `:session` (while refusing the startup-only `--dht-manifest` pin in favor of `(dao.space.dht/load-index ...)`); swapping out closes follower dials, the head board server, the UDP socket, and the directory lock, clearing `:session` and DHT modules.\n4. **Command surface**: **`(use-store \u003ctarget\u003e \u0026 \u003copts\u003e)` at the `yin\u003e` prompt only** — local shell/driver command (refused over remote `--port` `:op/eval`), accepting `\"mem\"` (or `:mem`), `\"file:\u003cdir\u003e\"`, and `\"dht:\u003cdir\u003e\"` with optional DHT join keyword args, without reading or writing `\u003cnode-dir\u003e/state.edn`.\n5. **Gambit boundary (owner ruling C4)**: **Honest capability degradation** — `(use-store \"mem\")` swaps memory stores while preserving Gambit's `jolt.ffi` and `dao.jing.mem` host modules; durable targets (`file:\u003cdir\u003e` and `dht:\u003cdir\u003e`) route through `dao.posix.file/realpath` (`host/gambit/yin/dao/posix/file.jolt`) during the `open-first` step to raise the exact C4 blocking-FFI refusal inline while the session survives.\n\n### Implementation Slice Plan\n\n1. **Slice 1 — Engine Quiescence \u0026 `mem` ↔ `file:\u003cdir\u003e` Store Swap**: Add `:quiesced?` tracking, `quiesced?`, `swap-refusal`, `install-store`, `swap-store`, and `use-store` across [store.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc), [repl.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc), [adapter.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc), [serve.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/serve.cljc), [driver.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc), and [main.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc), with unit coverage in [store_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc).\n2. **Slice 2 — DHT Composition Store Swap**: Add `parse-store-command` in [cli.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/shell/cli.cljc) (wired into `hooks` and [main.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc)) and synchronous `:bind-failed` detection in [dht.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc), with ring join/leave and failed-swap tests in `test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc`.\n3. **Slice 3 — Gambit Honest Degradation**: Update [yin.jolt](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/tools/jolt/host/gambit/yin/jolt/gambit/yin.jolt) and [yin-repl-session.sh](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/tools/jolt/test/gambit/yin-repl-session.sh) on the `gambit-ffi-p1` fork lineage (`mem`→`mem` swap + `file:`/`dht:` C4 refusal-then-survive on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64) and advance [jolt-toolchain.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/jolt-toolchain.edn) via the upgrade gate.\n4. **Slice 4 — Documentation \u0026 Tri-Host Landing Gate**: Update [yin.repl.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md) and [yin.repl.dao.space-index.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md), verify Gate A/B audits, and run the tri-host landing gate.\n\n### Findings File\n\n- [1795360785000-architect-store-swap-design.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yin-repl/1795360785000-architect-store-swap-design.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md)\n","duration_seconds":827.783932,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":387600,"output_tokens":61162,"thinking_tokens":41040,"cache_read_tokens":7293896,"total_tokens":448762}}
